WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.720
[Gavel knocking]

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.680
I thought congressional hearings were supposed

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.540
to educate lawmakers...

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.330
But today’s are mostly partisan bickering.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.340
Mr. Speaker, I do-

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.080
Chairman I have a –

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.290
Gentleman is not recognized.

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:12.080
I have a point of order

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:12.870
Gentleman is not recognized.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:13.870
I have a point of order though.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.840
I don’t see any education happening

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.770
a point of order --

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.690
Gentleman is not recognized.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.440
But members haven’t tried to learn things

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.460
at hearings for a long time.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.320
Maybe they don’t want to look as ignorant as

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.260
Senator Orrin Hatch did at this Facebook hearing.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.020
How do you sustain a business model in which

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.000
users don't pay for your service?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.100
Senator, we run ads.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.140
I see

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:40.240
You’d think they’d know basic facts

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.220
before asking questions.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.000
But no.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.260
I have a seven-year-old granddaughter who

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.160
picked up her phone before the election

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.880
Here congressman Steve King asks

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.510
Google’s CEO about an iPhone.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.280
But I'd ask you, how does that show up on

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:59.000
a seven year old's iPhone, who's playing a kid's game?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.760
Congressman, iPhone is made by a different company.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.080
Lately, they’re eager to attack big tech,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.160
especially Mark Zuckerberg, because he’s rich,

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.180
and Facebook’s so powerful.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.200
Last year he proposed a crypto currency called Libra.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.180
I actually don’t know if Libra is going to work,

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.200
but I believe it’s important to try new things.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.450
It is, so Congress should let him.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.820
Instead, they summon him to Washington where

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.920
Rep. Al Green grills him about groups he partners with:

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:32.410
How many are headed by women?

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.160
What does that have to do with Libra?

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.220
Congressman, I do not know the answer

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.580
Green, like many these days,

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:39.560
doesn’t want to learn anything.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.900
He wants to sneer and score points.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.980
How many of them are minorities, Mr. Zuckerberg?

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.300
Congressman, I do not know off

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:52.009
the top of my head.

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:56.420
Are there any members of the LGBTQ+ community?

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.270
Give me a break.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:00.040
These hearings have changed a lot since they

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.979
were invented by the very first Congress in 1789.

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:06.080
Founder George Mason said Members

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.740
“possess inquisitorial powers…”

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:12.099
to “inspect the Conduct of public offices.”

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:13.569
Are you stupid?

00:02:13.569 --> 00:02:16.140
But today members use their time to bully people.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.160
Mrs. DeVos, have you ever taken out a student loan?

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.580
Education secretary Betsy DeVos is a billionaire.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.560
Elizabeth Warren knows that yet she asks:

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.040
Have any of your children had to borrow money?

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.400
Warren’s wants to be seen bashing a rich Republican.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.480
They have been fortunate not to.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.220
Uh huh.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.380
Have you had any personal experience

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.400
with a Pell Grant?

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:38.100
Some in congress bash rich people and business…

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.780
for everything.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.150
Tim Sloan was boss of Wells Fargo.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.440
Mr. Sloan, why was the bank involved in

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.240
the caging of children?

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.020
Really? The bank helped cage children?

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.960
I don't know how to answer the question

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.500
because we weren't.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:55.740
Others grab TV face time to claim

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.800
they’re more virtuous than others.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.640
And I'm not going to sit here and allow this

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.300
committee to be used, to say that e-cigarettes,

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:06.000
vaping, Juul is not killing our people.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.800
Two last examples.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.100
When military personnel were being stationed

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.400
on the island of Guam,

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.849
Congressman Hank Johnson said this:

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:19.120
My fear is that the whole island will become

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:27.280
so overly populated, that it would tip over and capsize.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:28.549
Excuse me?

00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:30.920
We don’t anticipate that

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.240
Later Rep. Johnson said he was joking,

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.000
but it didn’t sound like he was joking.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.360
And then there was the time when

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.500
Congresswoman Maxine Waters grilled bankers

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.460
about student loan debt

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.450
What are you guys doing to help us with this

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.180
student loan debt?

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:46.650
Who would like to answer first?

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.709
Mr. Moynihan, big bank.

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:52.549
We stopped making student loans in 2007 or so.

00:03:52.549 --> 00:03:53.769
So you don't do it anymore.

00:03:53.769 --> 00:03:55.400
Mr. Corbat?

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.100
We actually ended student lending in 2009.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.100
Mr. Dimon?

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.700
When the government took over student lending

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.640
in 2010 or so we stopped doing all student lending.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.800
Is the chair of the Financial Services Committee

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.939
embarrassed that she didn’t know that

00:04:07.939 --> 00:04:09.500
at the direction of her party,

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.530
government took over student loans years ago?

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.420
I don’t know; her staff didn’t respond to our emails.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.820
Watching the hearings,

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.720
watching politicians score cheap points

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:23.220
and bully productive people

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:26.080
should make all of us want less government.

